  "title": "Are the Tigers Having the Most Confusing — and Secretly Consequential — Season Ever?",
  "subtitle": null,
  "byline": null,
  "publishedAt": null,
  "contentHtml": "<figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!9d2X!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa651250d-5204-4c0b-b7a7-5157d6f6552b_1900x1267.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n<img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!9d2X!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa651250d-5204-4c0b-b7a7-5157d6f6552b_1900x1267.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"971\" data-size=\"normal\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n\n</a><figcaption>MAY 12: (L-R) <strong>Dillon Dingler, manager A.J. Hinch, Spencer Torkelson, Kevin McGonigle and Gage Workman of the Detroit Tigers meet at the mound in the sixth inning against the New York Mets at Citi Field on May 12, 2026. </strong>(Evan Bernstein/Getty Images)</figcaption></figure>\n<p>No MLB team has had more “seasons” <em>within</em> the actual 2026 season than the Detroit Tigers. </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/subscribe?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p>\n<p>There was the <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-wbc-is-over-soon-the-real-baseball#:~:text=Here%E2%80%99s%20what%20those%20results%20look%20like%3A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">early-season version that was a division favorite</a>, harboring hopes of <a href=\"https://www.freep.com/story/sports/mlb/tigers/2026/02/19/tarik-skubal-contract-detroit-tigers-world-series/88697940007/?gnt-cfr=1&amp;gca-cat=p&amp;gca-uir=false&amp;gca-epti=z1119xxp119850n00----l001450c00----u002558e1119xxv004258&amp;gca-ft=235&amp;gca-ds=sophi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">making a “last dance” type of run</a> with Tarik Skubal in his likely Detroit finale.</p>\n<p>There was the version that <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/teams/tgl.cgi?team=DET&amp;t=p&amp;year=2026&amp;share=1.76#1-32-sum:players_standard_pitching\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">hung around .500</a> through the end of April, still keeping <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-mlb-elo-power-ratings-playoff\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">solid playoff odds</a> as <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/boxes/index.fcgi?date=2026-04-30\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">nobody else in the AL Central</a> broke away.</p>\n<p>There was the version that <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/teams/tgl.cgi?team=DET&amp;t=p&amp;year=2026&amp;share=0.18#27-60-sum:players_standard_pitching\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">went a ghastly 8-26</a> from late April through the end of May — producing the <a href=\"https://www.sports-reference.com/stathead/baseball/team-pitching-game-finder.cgi?request=1&amp;match=team_game_combined_season&amp;order_by=p_win_loss_perc&amp;timeframe=custom_timeframe&amp;date_min=2026-04-24&amp;date_max=2026-05-31\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">worst record in baseball</a> with <a href=\"https://www.prosportstransactions.com/baseball/Search/SearchResults.php?Player=skubal&amp;Team=tigers&amp;BeginDate=2026-01-01&amp;EndDate=&amp;DLChkBx=yes&amp;InjuriesChkBx=yes&amp;submit=Search\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Skubal mostly injured</a> — sending Detroit <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/boxes/index.fcgi?date=2026-05-31\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">tumbling to last place</a> and 3 percent playoff odds on June 1. </p>\n<p>There was the version that then won 30 of its next 50 games in June/July, producing <a href=\"https://www.sports-reference.com/stathead/baseball/team-pitching-game-finder.cgi?request=1&amp;match=team_game_combined_season&amp;order_by=p_win_loss_perc&amp;timeframe=custom_timeframe&amp;date_min=2026-06-01&amp;date_max=2026-07-31\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the fifth-</a><em><a href=\"https://www.sports-reference.com/stathead/baseball/team-pitching-game-finder.cgi?request=1&amp;match=team_game_combined_season&amp;order_by=p_win_loss_perc&amp;timeframe=custom_timeframe&amp;date_min=2026-06-01&amp;date_max=2026-07-31\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">best</a></em><a href=\"https://www.sports-reference.com/stathead/baseball/team-pitching-game-finder.cgi?request=1&amp;match=team_game_combined_season&amp;order_by=p_win_loss_perc&amp;timeframe=custom_timeframe&amp;date_min=2026-06-01&amp;date_max=2026-07-31\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> record in baseball</a>.</p>\n<p>There was the version whereby that performance still wasn’t enough to keep Skubal — who <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-dodgers-havent-ruined-baseball\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">was infamously dealt to the L.A. Dodgers</a> a <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-dodgers-havent-ruined-baseball\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">few days before the trade deadline</a>.</p>\n<p>And then there’s the current version, which is <a href=\"https://www.baseball-reference.com/teams/DET/2026.shtml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">still multiple games below .500</a> but also remains <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/mlb/standings/_/view/wild-card\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">one of the many teams within striking distance</a> of the American League’s final wild-card spot — yet can’t seem to decide whether it’s ready to make a run or finally fade away.</p>\n<p>Which is the <em>real </em>Tigers? Maybe all of the crazy variance is masking one of the best (yet also unluckiest and streakiest) teams in baseball, one whose refusal to play to its true talent level will end up having bizarrely outsized consequences for the rest of the sport.</p>\n<p>It sounds unlikely that a team who enters Friday with a 61-66 record on the season could secretly be among MLB’s top teams. But <a href=\"https://substack.com/@neilpaine/note/c-311769840\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">as I nodded to here</a>, Detroit has a seriously bizarre split between their actual record and underlying stats. </p>\n<p>\n          <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/are-the-tigers-having-the-most-confusing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>",
